{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>will rule</b> — on account of two [hands]." "<b>The diligent</b> — from <b>אָז תַחְרִיץ</b>, whose meaning is to move; that is, those who move about after their livelihood—their hand shall rule. And <b>the slack hand</b>—that deals deceitfully with people—it shall become a tribute to the diligent who rule. It is also possible that <b>חרוצים</b> means those who possess חרוץ, which is gold."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:26.731486357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}